{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03GS", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5df3f55062aae17428db5392399b292a638086cfa844e177ef6f1d1e9d6c8541", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe can use the algebraic version of Zariski's Main Theorem to show that\nthe set of points where a morphism is quasi-finite is open.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b3591de51dd00e682bf91e584e1f06167209445de6cedeb44e0d14ead5984830", "unit_id": "tag:03GS:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03GS", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nThe locally quasi-finite locus of a morphism is open\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\to S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-finite-points-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b4b105b70bc74543415d417045312462c66a18f27473c223dab70a3739984e9d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6dab988b1a5e4b5add69d9c6e942e3f60fe8004aa2aef9d0b649446a4a3634e5", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe set of points of <MATH_0002> where <MATH_0003> is quasi-finite is an open\n<MATH_0004>. The induced morphism <MATH_0005> is locally quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:de08be3a9b06a6722573e86b632d39c0aeff1687c88dcb2d076e5eed17b2afc5", "unit_id": "tag:01TI:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03GS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in U = \\Spec(A) \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$V = \\Spec(R) \\subset S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0006": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-quasi-finite}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{theorem-main-theorem}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-quasi-finite-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b2147d3b64bab9c72fdc200f6bd84b29fee74c7e410a7f89a59f9d234bc98f81", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c978bd0362d119c93d695ec2aa591b517640a4eacb1248e68ab2e50f02d80a79", "source_text": "Suppose <MATH_0001> is quasi-finite at <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004>\nbe affine opens as in Definition <REF_0001>.\nBy either Theorem <REF_0002> above or\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>,\nthe set of primes <MATH_0005> at which <MATH_0006> is quasi-finite\nis open in <MATH_0007>. Since these all correspond to points\nof <MATH_0008> where <MATH_0009> is quasi-finite we get the first statement.\nThe second statement is obvious.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f4923a5ab39323570bf5a9791f3c4407d74369870dc7051ac53d79e53ec150e2", "unit_id": "tag:01TI:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03GS", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-quasi-finite-separated-pass-through-finite}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:743027063d89d0a910136aabfe976eea4e5f3da58e27f4e7a34ca68a0f99bd07", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will improve the following lemma to general quasi-finite separated\nmorphisms later, see\nMore on Morphisms, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e8ef80fd965713adfc95e92dc49d639e158e70ba543a12111e65e1b53a35700a", "unit_id": "tag:03GS:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03GS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : Y \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nY \\ar[rd]_f \\ar[rr]_j & & Z \\ar[ld]^\\pi \\\\\n& X &\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$Z$", "MATH_0007": "$\\pi$", "MATH_0008": "$j$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-finite-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ba3ecd3bb57e7cf9213e014cd2aafc33a2a7f6a6a5ca9c128d805911a8a67be6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8ebe0a0b5c0d2f9f0656f4ba3e7b9dab9b367b6a1efd8bbb933e2693170ad4dd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nAssume\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> are affine, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0004> is quasi-finite.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen there exists a diagram\n<MATH_0005>\nwith <MATH_0006> affine, <MATH_0007> finite and <MATH_0008> an open immersion.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:16290856b07cc53676e76d029441ee8535d47b0a3c7ddf042a4a9ddc266e089d", "unit_id": "tag:03GU:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03GS", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-quasi-finite-open-integral-closure}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8ff7e21653097f2a92ce40a393870381eb36d246b138d19b0567b7da28e32f53", "source_text": "This is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>\nreformulated in the language of schemes.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4555101bc73b2510dca7bbfdf1f57b79a75f9044c7cb34a83ca3af7f7610f231", "unit_id": "tag:03GU:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03GS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : Y \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\subset Y$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$f(T) \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-image-nowhere-dense-quasi-finite}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5e005e67879a0527c69772b2c02a8ce7b3326a74cedf3a63a395beeb00007f86", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:47a222a50c4ed028a2ce9eca168bd8aed9bca9aa38452a779c5651706d730f57", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-finite morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a closed nowhere dense subset of <MATH_0003>.\nThen <MATH_0004> is a nowhere dense subset of <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ac0650935a21e9e6c0d3494a2db91b888c8e7c1ebeaf0ddbde55219140fd8e82", "unit_id": "tag:03J2:statement"}
